          "status": "approved",
          "reason": "Actual Bernoulli laws, exact integrals and a strict canonical binEntropy inequality establish the comparison. Real logarithm enclosures certify nearest-six-decimal accuracy. Less predictable is the explanatory reading of larger Shannon entropy here, not an independent empirical guarantee."
        },
        {
          "source_clause": "Natural logs give nats; base-two logs express the same information in bits.",
          "kind": "mathematical_conclusion",
          "lean_declarations": [
